md('02_existing_universe_audit.md','''# Existing implementation audit and reuse
28 receipt-pinned code/test/consumer files reviewed; full identities and caller hits are in support/source-audit.json. Backfill scripts were read as code only, never executed against original source roots.

| Existing path/function | Observed limitation and consumer | Disposition / new proof |
|---|---|---|
| track_b/universe_manager.py:get_universe | Effective/removal dates only; no independent knowledge cutoff; missing InstrumentMaster silently continues; delisting filter affects returned rows. Used by legacy API/pipeline/proofs. | Preserve legacy; opt-in OD08 uses OD06 knowledge-aware identity. U06/U07/I03/I04. |
| remove_membership | Mutates prior removal dates, losing original knowledge state. | Append-only MembershipRevision wrapper and SQLite parent constraint. U07-U10/P06. |
| reconstruct_pre2010 | Sorts all qualifying DataFrame rows by market_cap and takes top N; repeated observations can duplicate a security; no evidenced availability or complete methodology proof. | Preserve legacy risk; provisional ranking rejects duplicate identities and unavailable inputs. R01/R02. |
| _scan_symbol_isin_map / seed helpers | Raw ZIP traversal and last-write dictionary have no bitemporal semantics. | Never called; source_backfill refusal reused and tested. |
| MembershipClaim/StrictUniverse | Accounts for supplied rows but cannot establish authentic completeness. Legacy correction validator requires identical valid bounds. | Reuse MembershipClaim unchanged inside new wrapper; correction lineage permits changed valid boundaries; coverage independent. C01-C05/U08. |
| PersistentRepository | OD06 identity/calendar storage and source authority remain valid; existing membership schema lacks OD08 coverage/policy/context semantics. | Reuse typed snapshots, SQLAlchemy transaction/ownership conventions and exact evidence identities. No production migration. |

MemoryIdentityRepository, EvidenceAuthority, VerifiedCalendar, legacy_universe_inventory and OD07 v2 contracts are reused. No new dependency, paid service or external data framework. Python standard library and existing SQLAlchemy/SQLite suffice. These audit findings are code-level facts, not verified historical financial discrepancies. New tests use anonymous controls; legacy financial expectations stay unchanged.''')
md('03_universe_domain_contract.md','''# Versioned universe domain
UniverseDefinition separates OFFICIAL_INDEX, EXCHANGE_LISTED_UNIVERSE, RESEARCH_ELIGIBLE_UNIVERSE, PROVISIONAL_RECONSTRUCTION and CUSTOM_POLICY_UNIVERSE. It declares SECURITY/LISTING granularity, methodology, source/venue scopes, valid and known intervals, evidence and version. Definition and coverage sequences must be actual tuples; mutable lists refuse.

MembershipRevision wraps the existing OD06 MembershipClaim instead of replacing it. It adds opaque event/revision lineage, source/artifact/record IDs, optional stable security/listing, announcement/publication/ingestion, event type, revision and effective convention. Original symbol/series/ISIN/exchange remain in the claim. Unknown stable identity remains absent. EXPLICIT_TIMESTAMP retains aware effective/removal instants; UNKNOWN convention blocks use. No official identities or sessions invented.''')
md('04_bitemporal_membership_contract.md','''# Independent valid and knowledge time
get_universe_as_of requires explicit valid date or aware timestamp, aware known cutoff, consumer policy and exact source_snapshot_id. Date and knowledge intervals are half-open. Corrections preserve opaque economic-event lineage while allowing changed valid dates, identity and classification. Parent must exist, revision increment one, knowledge strictly increase; duplicate/competing children refuse. Cancellation supersedes prior knowledge without rewriting the parent.

Source-date semantics do not invent a market-open instant. Explicit timestamps use exact economic start/end; date-only queries over timestamp-specific claims remain blocked for availability. Exchange-local business date uses Asia/Kolkata, independent of host timezone. SQL uses UTC-normalized knowledge/effective timestamps.

Known future announcements are separate upcoming outputs, never current constituents. Unknown availability, future publication/announcement and denied sources remain explicit. Future-known revisions cannot change an earlier snapshot digest. Historical states can be replayed and compared; no current-clock fallback.''')
md('05_information_availability_contract.md','''# Information availability
AvailabilityObservation retains economic, observed, published, known and ingested times, completed interval, exact artifact/record, listing, units/bases, evidence and version. Unknown required availability or incomplete intervals block. Publication, observed time and completed interval may not exceed cutoff. Ingestion is not substituted for publication or known time.

STRICT uses EvidenceAuthority and the unchanged source-rights register. Conservative treatment is a separate policy requiring an explicit bound, reviewed semantics and independently authorized policy evidence under STRICT. Caller-provided delays/references and canaries cannot self-authorize it. No default delay.

Intraday decisions cannot use eventual daily close/volume or future adjustment information. Zero-valued anonymous observations are software bookkeeping controls, not market observations or financial-accuracy evidence.''')
md('06_survivorship_bias_controls.md','''# Historical identity without survivor filtering
Resolve the reported identifier at its applicable historical boundary, then follow stable listing/security through OD06. Renames and series changes do not require an old ticker to remain current. Reused symbols and exchanges do not merge identities. Missing masters, ambiguity and unknown continuity remain visible.

Delisted or suspended securities may remain historical constituents. Membership differs from tradability and execution. SECURITY duplicates remain conflicting rather than choosing an arbitrary listing; LISTING granularity retains separately declared listings. No ranking by today's active list.

A per-query index builds complete listing-lineage views once and reuses the existing resolver. The negative-first budget test reproduced18 candidate examinations for3 members; indexed views remove repeated full-ledger work without discarding parents or ambiguity.''')
md('07_historical_coverage_contract.md','''# Coverage is independent from selected accounting
UniverseCoverage records exact scope, method, source artifact, independent reference, valid/known bounds, expected identities/count, snapshot/transition classification and authority. States are COMPLETE_VERIFIED, COMPLETE_FOR_DECLARED_NON_MARKET_SCOPE, PARTIAL, PROVISIONAL, UNKNOWN, CONFLICTING and SOURCE_BLOCKED.

A SNAPSHOT covers one explicit date only. Interval coverage needs independently declared starting/ending sets, an ending reference and exact intervening ADD/REMOVE transitions bound to revisions and boundaries. Missing transitions remain PARTIAL; incorrect endpoints, identities or duplicates conflict. No indefinite forward-fill.

COMPLETE_VERIFIED cannot come from non-market controls. Actual authentic coverage remains BLOCKED_REAL_DATA. Empty-with-no-coverage is UNKNOWN, not proof of absence. Empty controlled coverage cannot confer financial acceptance. Two snapshots alone do not prove complete change history.''')
md('08_exact_constituent_reconciliation.md','''# Exact identities, not counts
Reconciliation returns expected-minus-actual, actual-minus-expected, matching identities, duplicates and unresolved revisions. Same-count wrong sets fail. Unknown symbols cannot substitute for mismatched securities. Expected control sets are explicit literal tuples in tests, never generated by the production query.

Every selected revision has exactly one primary decision. Included, excluded, unresolved, blocked, conflicting and provisional decisions reconcile to selected count. Research/liquidity/tradability/execution diagnostics accompany the primary decision. Exclusion never erases underlying membership. Complete selected accounting cannot certify source coverage.''')
md('09_consumer_eligibility_policies.md','''# Consumer policies remain separate
MEMBERSHIP returns source-selected accounting without strategy filters. RESEARCH adds declared observation/quality/adjustment requirements. LIQUIDITY applies a versioned window and thresholds. EXECUTION consumes bound raw-basis OD07 execution eligibility.

No universal financial threshold is invented. Research exclusions do not alter official membership. Later unavailable observations or future history cannot decide earlier eligibility. PROVISIONAL_ONLY remains provisional regardless of confidence. Financial and execution acceptance flags remain false pending separate authentic-source/release gates.''')
md('10_liquidity_and_tradability_contract.md','''# Completed-session liquidity and tradability
LiquidityPolicy pins lookback sessions, minimum completed count, average-volume/median-turnover thresholds, observation coverage, currency, unit and bases. Only verified completed sessions enter the window. Unknown coverage or closing time blocks; no weekday approximation. Duplicate listing-session observations block. Missing volume differs from zero; real zero remains valid under the policy. Missing sessions are reported, not silently skipped. Currency/units/bases must match; adjusted volume requires OD07 context.

Decimal calculations use the existing pinned arithmetic context. Average volume and median turnover use time-eligible observations. Strict execution also needs lifecycle/session/lot/settlement/restriction and availability inputs supplied through OD07. CALCULATED or raw price alone is not tradability. No orders or simulated trading.''')
md('11_OD07_context_integration.md','''# OD07 v2 integration
Consume RawObservation, ReferenceObservation, HistorySnapshot, ParameterSet, BasisPolicy, PinnedCalculation and BoundResult. Preserve raw/result/context/history/identity/calendar/authority digests, basis, cutoff, profile and version. Positive structural integration replays an actual typed OD07 calculation. Wrong profile, absent pin, future cutoff or mismatched listing refuse.

Membership does not require adjusted history. Conventional forward never substitutes the v1 inverse comparison. Execution requires raw-unadjusted EXECUTION profile and independently bound true execution eligibility; non-market results cannot qualify.

The payload codec extends OD07 encoding for tuples/dictionaries. Authority objects are represented only by exact state digests; reconstruction requires an independently configured matching authority or the exact unconfigured state. This serializes no permission grant. Configured publisher-positive financial acceptance remains externally blocked.''')
md('12_provisional_reconstruction_contract.md','''# Provisional ranking only
Inputs are unique stable member IDs, finite Decimal metric, evidenced observation and explicit cutoff. Duplicate members refuse before ranking. Unavailable inputs and unresolved identities are excluded with reasons. Metric-descending, opaque-ID ascending ties are an explicit custom policy, not an official methodology.

All reconstruction remains RECONSTRUCTED_PROVISIONAL. No constituents, market-cap histories or original archives were generated/read. Anonymous scalar controls prove ordering only. Original reconstruct_pre2010 remains unchanged and is not authoritative historical acceptance.''')
md('13_snapshot_admission_and_integrity.md','''# Immutable snapshots and independently reconciled admission
Bind definition, valid/known query, source snapshot, visible membership ledger, coverage, consumer/availability/liquidity policies, relevant identity/calendar/authority and OD07 contexts. Irrelevant future-known inputs do not enter earlier identities. Input ordering is canonicalized; decisions/reasons have deterministic digests.

Repository pinning independently selects required revisions using indexed SQL temporal predicates and reconciles every selected decision. Full visible persisted membership and coverage ledgers must match supplied inputs; omitted members or coverage refuse. Definition, policy and evidence bytes must match stored records. Verify context checksum before admission/replay. Submitted snapshot must match immutable pinned expectation; altered decisions, digests and references refuse atomically.

This is trusted internal-service admission plus independent SQL accounting, not protection against unrestricted same-process code or a DB administrator. Separate literal-set tests verify semantics. No independent human review claimed.''')
md('14_persistence_and_rollback.md','''# Disposable SQLAlchemy/SQLite
Nine additive tables: schema, definition, membership, coverage, availability, policy, context, snapshot and decision. Foreign keys bind definition/parent/policy/context/snapshot/member. Unique parent serializes corrections. Append-only UPDATE/DELETE triggers, BEGIN IMMEDIATE, identical retries and changed-ID refusal. Event/as-of indexes avoid full-ledger validation per append.

Actual tests: memory/file-backed insert/reopen, replay after restart, immutable history, two concurrent connections (one commit/one refusal), controlled rollback, FK refusal, fresh migration, empty rollback and nonempty refusal. Unknown schema/version refuses. No operational migration or destructive history rewrite.

OD06/OD07 are separate upstream stores: contexts bind immutable typed snapshots and authority state. No distributed transaction or implicit live refresh. Production needs separate ownership, backup/restore, upstream-consistency and migration rehearsal. Rollback disables the opt-in path while preserving accepted evidence; no automatic cleanup.''')
